{title: 422 - Marching to Zion}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #422 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 422}
{meta: category Doctrines - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Come ye that [C7]love the [F]Lord, and let your joys be [C]known,
Join [F]in a song with [Bb]sweet accord, Join [C]in a song with [G]sweet [G7]ac[C]cord.
And [F]thus [C]sur[F]round the [Gm7]throne, and [F]thus sur[C7]round the [F]throne.
[F]We&#39;re marching to Zion, beautiful, beauti[C]ful Zion;
We&#39[F];re marching upward[Bb] to Zion; [F]the beauti[C7]ful city[F] of God
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[F]We're [C7]marching [F]to [C]Zion,
[F][Bb]Beautiful, [C][G]beautiful [G7][C]Zion;
[F][C]We're [F]marching [Gm7][F]upward [C7]to [F]Zion,
[F]The beautiful [C]city of God.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Let [C7]those [F]refuse [C]to sing
[F][Bb]Who [C]never [G]knew [G7]our [C]God;
[F][C]But [F]children [Gm7]of [F]the [C7]heav'nly [F]King,
[F]But children of [C]the heav'nly King
[F]May [Bb]speak [F]their [C7]joys [F]abroad,
[F]May [C7]speak [F]their [C]joys abroad.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]The [C7]hill [F]of [C]Zion yields
[F][Bb]A [C]thousand [G][G7]sacred [C]sweets
[F][C]Before [F]we [Gm7]reach [F]the [C7]heav'nly [F]fields,
[F]Before we reach [C]the heav'nly fields
[F]Or [Bb]walk [F]the [C7]golden [F]streets,
[F]Or [C7]walk [F]the [C]golden streets.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]Then [C7]let [F]our [C]songs abound
[F][Bb]And [C]ev'ry [G]tear [G7]be [C]dry;
[F][C]We're [F]marching [Gm7][F]thru [C7]Immanuel's [F]ground,
[F]We're marching [C]thru Immanuel's ground
[F]To [Bb]fairer [F]worlds [C7]on [F]high,
[F]To [C7]fairer [F]worlds [C]on high.
{end_of_verse}
